  "point": "Random guessing scores 6%. The plain add-only memory reaches only 57%: because it just sums every write, when a key appears several times it ends up holding a blur of all that key's values and can't say which was latest. The erase-first memory reaches 100% \u2014 writing each value in place of the old one keeps only the current answer. The learned forget dial reaches 100%. The gap is the whole argument: being able to overwrite isn't polish, it's what makes 'remember the latest value' learnable at all."
